ent"><article class=3D"style_learnContent__K5K7M"><header><h1>LRU Cache</h1=
></header><div class=3D"style_problemDescription__T4cPe"><p>Design and impl=
ement a data structure for the Least Recently Used (LRU) cache that support=
s the following operations:</p><ul>
<li><code>LRUCache(capacity: int)</code>: Initialize an LRU cache with the =
specified capacity.</li>
<li><code>get(key: int) -&gt; int</code>: Return the value associated with =
a key. Return -1 if the key doesn't exist.</li>
<li><code>put(key: int, value: int) -&gt; None</code>: Add a key and its va=
lue to the cache. If adding the key would result in the cache exceeding its=
 size capacity, <strong>evict the least recently used element</strong>. If =
the key already exists in the cache, update its value.</li>
</ul><h4 id=3D"example">Example:</h4><pre><code class=3D"hljs language-pyth=
on">Input: [
  put(<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">100=
</span>),
  put(<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">250=
</span>),
  get(<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>),
  put(<span class=3D"hljs-number">4</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">300=
</span>),
  put(<span class=3D"hljs-number">3</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">200=
</span>),
  get(<span class=3D"hljs-number">4</span>),
  get(<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>),
],
  capacity =3D <span class=3D"hljs-number">3</span>
Output: [<span class=3D"hljs-number">250</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number=
">300</span>, -<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>]
</code></pre><p>Explanation:</p><pre><code class=3D"hljs language-python">p=
ut(<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">100</s=
pan>)  <span class=3D"hljs-comment"># cache is[1: 100]</span>
put(<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">250</=
span>)  <span class=3D"hljs-comment"># cache is[1: 100, 2: 250]</span>
get(<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>)       <span class=3D"hljs-comment=
"># return 250</span>
put(<span class=3D"hljs-number">4</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">300</=
span>)  <span class=3D"hljs-comment"># cache is[1: 100, 2: 250, 4: 300]t</s=
pan>
put(<span class=3D"hljs-number">3</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">200</=
span>)  <span class=3D"hljs-comment"># cache is[2: 250, 4: 300, 3: 200]</sp=
an>
get(<span class=3D"hljs-number">4</span>)       <span class=3D"hljs-comment=
"># return 300</span>
get(<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>)       <span class=3D"hljs-comment=
"># key 1 was evicted when adding key 3 due to the capacity</span>
             <span class=3D"hljs-comment"># limit: return -1</span>
</code></pre><h4 id=3D"constraints">Constraints:</h4><ul>
<li>
<p>All keys and values are positive integers.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The cache capacity is positive.</p>
</li>
</ul></div>
<h2 id=3D"intuition">Intuition</h2>
<p>When presented with a design problem, the first steps usually involve un=
derstanding the problem and deciding which data structures to use. Let's st=
art by understanding how an LRU cache works at a high level.</p>
<p>Consider the LRU cache described below. It currently holds 3 elements an=
d has reached full capacity. Assume that in this representation, the key-va=
lue pairs are ordered from the least recently used (left) to the most recen=
tly used (right):</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
;"><img alt=3D"Image represents a visual depiction of a Least Recently Used=
 (LRU) cache with a capacity of 3.  The main component is a rectangular box=
 representing the cache, divided into three smaller rectangular cells. Each=
 cell contains a pair of numbers; the first represents a key (1, 2, or 4), =
and the second represents an associated value (100, 250, or 300).  The cell=
s are arranged horizontally within the larger cache box, with the cell cont=
aining '1 | 100' on the left, representing the least recently used item, an=
d the cell containing '4 | 300' on the right, representing the most recentl=
y used item.  An arrow extends from the left edge of the cache box to the r=
ight, labeled 'least recently used' on the left and 'most recently used' on=
 the right, explicitly indicating the order of usage within the cache.  The=
 text 'capacity =3D 3' above the cache box specifies the maximum number of =
key-value pairs the cache can hold." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"311" height=
=3D"105" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D"1" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/i=
mages/courses/coding-patterns/linked-lists/lru-cache/image-03-04-1-GMOZULLA=
.svg" style=3D"color: transparent;"></div></figure>
<hr>
<p>Let's try putting a new key-value pair into the cache:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
;"><img alt=3D"The image represents a data structure, likely a fixed-size a=
